{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1486341-mind-sphere-increasing-ability-scores","id":1486341,"title":"Mind Sphere Increasing Ability Scores","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-07-13T07:28:48-07:00","id":1486341,"title":"Mind Sphere Increasing Ability Scores","content":"I posted this question on the Mage Discord to mixed responses so I thought I would post this question here as well.<br /> <br /> Reading the Technocracy book, they have a device called the &quot;Sleepteacher&quot;. It basically lets you buy ranks in an Ability without the need to train them in game. It got me thinking about the Mind Sphere in general, and how it would interact with Abilities. Someone's skill at something is basically housed in the long term memory portion of the brain, meaning most of it is mental. It's why people who get short term amnesia can still remember how to drive a car and things like that. Mechanically we know the Mind Sphere can raise your Mental Attributes just like Life can raise Physical Attributes. Would Mind be able to temporarily raise Ability scores though? On one hand it feels like it should be able to since how strongly someone's skills are linked to their memory, but nothing in the game (Other than the Sleepteacher) ever really talks about Spheres affecting Abilities at all.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7550-vulcan7200","name":"Vulcan7200","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-13T07:52:28-07:00","id":1486343,"title":"","content":"There are no rules that would allow to do that, AFAIK. So, by RAW, I don't think there's a clear way to do so. In general, Mage handless these by lowering difficulties - the result often looks the same: More success on a roll, and whatever that means. So, one could argue that's not even necessary for general purposes<br /> <br /> But I get that in some situations one could be better than then other, and in general it's frustrationg when the system refuses to engage with a mechanic for no specified reason (if you have free-form mechanics to raise one set of Traits, it's only natural to think about raising others).<br /> <br /> I would allow it <i>conditionally </i>depending on the Ability, and the explanation given. Problem is, unlike Attributes, there's no clear divide between the &quot;mental&quot; and the &quot;physical&quot; or even social aspects of an Ability (which ties well to the system allowing varied combinations of Attribute + Ability).<br /> <br /> For instance, what Brawl does needs you to train your body and your mind. Your body can be shaped by the hardcore training to figth, giving you physical capabilities (muscle memory, muscles tied to punching power) that an equaly athletic person may not have - this isn't something Mind can give you.<br /> While things like &quot;following the rithm of your opponent&quot; would seem more tied to Perception or Wits, conceptually, but in a way that an equally perceptive scientist could lack.<br /> <br /> Knowledges seem mental, but also may have physical aspects (Medicine to be a surgeon needs trained hands, Dexterity) or involve social aspects (Albeit these could be still handled by Mind, most likely, so it's a bit nonsensical)<br /> <br /> So, I would determine the Spheres and the levels to raise an Ability by looking at the Ability and the Rote, rather than grant one for all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 07-13-2022, 11:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-13T07:59:20-07:00","id":1486344,"title":"","content":"The way I see it, Attributes represent the aptitude, while Abilities are trained. Meaning, while it is certainly possible to magically increase your aptitude for something, increasing your learned Abilities is a different story. You would have to magically manifest knowledge, practice, and talent to raise the stats for an Ability. That's difficult.*<br /> <br /> The Sleepteacher Device is basically <a href=\"https://youtu.be/2kArCRjT29w?t=84\" target=\"_blank\">Dexter's Omelette Du Fromage</a> record player: a thing that implants knowledge into your brain while you're sleeping, something that is claimed to work IRL by some. But it doesn't create the knowledge from nil, it just blasts your brain with it until it soaks it up.<br /> <br /> There are ways to use Mind for enhanced learning, though. By increasing your Attributes (ie, aptitude) it becomes easier to learn and may shorten the time to do so. You could also use it to transplant knowledge from someone to yourself. I don't recall if there's a rote for this atm, but I think I remember something like that as an example in one of the books.<br /> <br /> There's also the option to use knowledge of a past incarnation (through the Past Lives Background). But in all cases, knowledge doesn't come from the void. It seems one of the fundamental rules is that you have to put the effort in.<br /> <br /> *Edit: To clarify 'difficult'. There's a paradox in summoning up knowledge of something you don't know. It gets a bit hazy with Divinations here, but generally I would say they are different processes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":27477,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","user":"voidshaper","date":". 07-13-2022, 11:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-13T09:18:52-07:00","id":1486346,"title":"","content":"I would say the knowledge has to be <i>known</i> by someone. If you have acolytes or extraordinary citizens with those Abilities, you could access them through a Mind-Link. There was actually an <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6rcWWYSSo6w\" target=\"_blank\">experiment</a> done with rats where one rat was able to learn from the experience of another because their brains were linked by wires. Otherwise, take the Dream Background. It's pretty flexible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-14T08:52:45-07:00","id":1486425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1486341-mind-sphere-increasing-ability-scores?p=1486343#post1486343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are no rules that would allow to do that, AFAIK. So, by RAW, I don't think there's a clear way to do so. In general, Mage handless these by lowering difficulties - the result often looks the same: More success on a roll, and whatever that means. So, one could argue that's not even necessary for general purposes<br /> <br /> But I get that in some situations one could be better than then other, and in general it's frustrationg when the system refuses to engage with a mechanic for no specified reason (if you have free-form mechanics to raise one set of Traits, it's only natural to think about raising others).<br /> <br /> I would allow it <i>conditionally </i>depending on the Ability, and the explanation given. Problem is, unlike Attributes, there's no clear divide between the &amp;quot;mental&amp;quot; and the &amp;quot;physical&amp;quot; or even social aspects of an Ability (which ties well to the system allowing varied combinations of Attribute + Ability).<br /> <br /> For instance, what Brawl does needs you to train your body and your mind. Your body can be shaped by the hardcore training to figth, giving you physical capabilities (muscle memory, muscles tied to punching power) that an equaly athletic person may not have - this isn't something Mind can give you.<br /> While things like &amp;quot;following the rithm of your opponent&amp;quot; would seem more tied to Perception or Wits, conceptually, but in a way that an equally perceptive scientist could lack.<br /> <br /> Knowledges seem mental, but also may have physical aspects (Medicine to be a surgeon needs trained hands, Dexterity) or involve social aspects (Albeit these could be still handled by Mind, most likely, so it's a bit nonsensical)<br /> <br /> So, I would determine the Spheres and the levels to raise an Ability by looking at the Ability and the Rote, rather than grant one for all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dexterity however is a MENTAL attribute, not a physical one. Your muscles do NOT have a memory of their own, the only thing they have is strengh, speed and flexibility. Reflexes and motor coordination thou are all inside the nervous system, therefore it's all in the mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-14T09:02:46-07:00","id":1486427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vulcan7200</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1486341-mind-sphere-increasing-ability-scores#post1486341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I posted this question on the Mage Discord to mixed responses so I thought I would post this question here as well.<br /> <br /> Reading the Technocracy book, they have a device called the &amp;quot;Sleepteacher&amp;quot;. It basically lets you buy ranks in an Ability without the need to train them in game. It got me thinking about the Mind Sphere in general, and how it would interact with Abilities. Someone's skill at something is basically housed in the long term memory portion of the brain, meaning most of it is mental. It's why people who get short term amnesia can still remember how to drive a car and things like that. Mechanically we know the Mind Sphere can raise your Mental Attributes just like Life can raise Physical Attributes. Would Mind be able to temporarily raise Ability scores though? On one hand it feels like it should be able to since how strongly someone's skills are linked to their memory, but nothing in the game (Other than the Sleepteacher) ever really talks about Spheres affecting Abilities at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do allow Mind to be used to raise skill - there are two ways to do it thou: the easy and the hard way.<br /> <br /> The easy way is, you COPY the skills from someone who has them. Therefore, if you wanna Stealth 5, you need to &quot;download&quot; it from someone who has it. So, make a Mind 3 effect to &quot;transfer&quot; such knowledge between minds.<br /> <br /> The hard way is to construct such knowledge from the ground up using simulations. For that, you need Entropy 5 (and Mind 3 afterwards to &quot;download&quot; it to yourself).<br /> <br /> It goes almost without saying that the VA and Iteration X are the best at this. The VA can literally &quot;download&quot; skills and copy them into hardrives for later use with Prime 2. <br /> <br /> In my games, the VA have extensive digital &quot;libraries&quot; of skills, so all they have to do is access the Digital Web and promptly dowload whatever they need - and yes, it's a massive advantage for the VAs born from their unique culture. VA members routinely &quot;upload&quot; new useful skills into their library, whenever they happen to find them, further increasing their overall collection.<br /> <br /> And, masters of Entropy can simply create the knowledge out of the blue - which they can later on use at will, if they go into the trouble of storaging the skills somewhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-14T09:06:38-07:00","id":1486428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1486341-mind-sphere-increasing-ability-scores?p=1486344#post1486344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The way I see it, Attributes represent the aptitude, while Abilities are trained. Meaning, while it is certainly possible to magically increase your aptitude for something, increasing your learned Abilities is a different story. You would have to magically manifest knowledge, practice, and talent to raise the stats for an Ability. That's difficult.*<br /> <br /> The Sleepteacher Device is basically <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">https://youtu.be/2kArCRjT29w?t=84&amp;quot;]Dexter's</a> Omelette Du Fromage[/URL] record player: a thing that implants knowledge into your brain while you're sleeping, something that is claimed to work IRL by some. But it doesn't create the knowledge from nil, it just blasts your brain with it until it soaks it up.<br /> <br /> There are ways to use Mind for enhanced learning, though. By increasing your Attributes (ie, aptitude) it becomes easier to learn and may shorten the time to do so. You could also use it to transplant knowledge from someone to yourself. I don't recall if there's a rote for this atm, but I think I remember something like that as an example in one of the books.<br /> <br /> There's also the option to use knowledge of a past incarnation (through the Past Lives Background). But in all cases, knowledge doesn't come from the void. It seems one of the fundamental rules is that you have to put the effort in.<br /> <br /> *Edit: To clarify 'difficult'. There's a paradox in summoning up knowledge of something you don't know. It gets a bit hazy with Divinations here, but generally I would say they are different processes.</div> </div> </div> </div>With Entropy 5 you can actually create knowledge &quot;from the Void&quot;. You can indeed will it to be out of nowhere just by pure happenstance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-14T09:36:58-07:00","id":1486431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1486341-mind-sphere-increasing-ability-scores?p=1486425#post1486425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Dexterity however is a MENTAL attribute, not a physical one. Your muscles do NOT have a memory of their own, the only thing they have is strengh, speed and flexibility. Reflexes and motor coordination thou are all inside the nervous system, therefore it's all in the mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that such proposal may cause undesirable consequences elsewhere. Dexterity it's represented by the rules as a Physical Attribute, in general Sphere text reffers to these denominations when they talk about stuff<br /> <br /> Mind and Life are sepparate Spheres in the rules. We have to work with that, barring a major change on the system that I don't think it's warranted here. Saying that the &quot;nervous system&quot; - clearly part of your biology - it's part of the &quot;Mind Sphere&quot; would generate some oddities in the rules.As shown by your very example:<br /> <br /> Raising Dexterity it's normaly Life 3 (altering the &quot;nervous system&quot; could be the Technomancer's way of doing so, while still using Life. After all, that system it's part of your biology, so, why not?), but apparently you can do it much better with Mind from now on, as Mind 1 it's enough to raise Mental Attributes. IDK if one wants to allow that kind of thing","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 07-14-2022, 12:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-14T09:57:48-07:00","id":1486436,"title":"","content":"I did a poor job of pointing out the paradox of creating knowledge in my previous post, let me try with a parable:<br /> <br /> Say you want to conjure an apple. Easy, you know apples, their flavor, shape, and texture.<br /> <br /> Now, I tell you to conjure a kumquat, and let's assume you never heard of kumquats, let alone ate one, or even know what the hell they are. I would say you could not cast that simple conjuration, because you wouldn't even be able to understand what I want. The magic itself doesn't know, your spell doesn't have a target you can Will into.<br /> <br /> Taking that example to knowledge, how are you going to create the knowledge of, say, martial arts if you don't know about martial arts in the first place? Even if you know basics (Brawl 3) and want to increase that, <i>how would you know what you want to be able to know</i>?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1486341-mind-sphere-increasing-ability-scores?p=1486428#post1486428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With Entropy 5 you can actually create knowledge &quot;from the Void&quot;. You can indeed will it to be out of nowhere just by pure happenstance.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can? Either we have a very different interpretation of Entropy, or I'm missing a reference in the books you have and I do not. Entropy 5 + Mind (for me) is affecting conceptual thoughts in a manner that is consistent with Fate or, well, entropy. Changing outlooks, supercharging creativity, inspirations, and so on.<br /> <br /> Edit: Oh i see, you're using Entropy 5 to basically re-invent everything on the fly based on what you know already. That could work I guess, but would probably be a pretty steep roll.<br /> <br /> I agree though that once you have a source for the knowledge, it becomes much easier to Will it into your brain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":27477,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","user":"voidshaper","date":". 07-14-2022, 01:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-14T10:17:24-07:00","id":1486440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1486341-mind-sphere-increasing-ability-scores?p=1486436#post1486436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I did a poor job of pointing out the paradox of creating knowledge in my previous post, let me try with a parable:<br /> Say you want to conjure an apple. Easy, you know apples, their flavor, shape, and texture.<br /> <br /> Now, I tell you to conjure a kumquat, and let's assume you never heard of kumquats, let alone ate one, or even know what the hell they are. I would say you could not cast that simple conjuration, because you wouldn't even be able to understand what I want. The magic itself doesn't know, your spell doesn't have a target you can Will into.</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely, You need to know what you create. Trying to Mind 3/Prime 2 knowledge would be futile<br /> <br /> That being said, magick could be able to procure knowledge, if you know where to search, and, as you said &quot;blast your brain&quot; with it (or otherwise incorporate). Several examples were given. Like the &quot;copy it from another&quot; example: I don't know much martial arts, but will trust the famous Sifu down there knows. That's how normal people gains those dots - magick would just resolve the mundane ways in a different fashion<br /> <br /> I would add that maybe you can extract knowledge from the High Umbra, with Cosmology and a bit of knowledge on the subject to seek the right realms. That may be one way to gain levels above 5 (something rather hard to find in other people). Albeit I would imagine it would take arround Mind 4 (or maybe less, with some Spirit)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 07-14-2022, 01:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-14T11:08:57-07:00","id":1486448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1486341-mind-sphere-increasing-ability-scores?p=1486440#post1486440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That being said, magick could be able to procure knowledge, if you know where to search, and, as you said &quot;blast your brain&quot; with it (or otherwise incorporate). Several examples were given. Like the &quot;copy it from another&quot; example: I don't know much martial arts, but will trust the famous Sifu down there knows. That's how normal people gains those dots - magick would just resolve the mundane ways in a different fashion</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. This conversation made me look into the <i>Lesser Key of Salomon</i> again, because that's basically what it's concerned with. With the <i>Ars Goetia</i> you summon spirits to learn from them, getting a knowledge transfer. With the <i>Ars Notoria</i>, you can invoke spiritual aid for learning, basically using Mind 1 under a theurgic guise.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1486341-mind-sphere-increasing-ability-scores?p=1486440#post1486440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would add that maybe you can extract knowledge from the High Umbra, with Cosmology and a bit of knowledge on the subject to seek the right realms. That may be one way to gain levels above 5 (something rather hard to find in other people). Albeit I would imagine it would take arround Mind 4 (or maybe less, with some Spirit)</div> </div> </div> </div> That's what the Epiphamies are made for, imo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-14T12:30:51-07:00","id":1486455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1486341-mind-sphere-increasing-ability-scores?p=1486431#post1486431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think that such proposal may cause undesirable consequences elsewhere. Dexterity it's represented by the rules as a Physical Attribute, in general Sphere text reffers to these denominations when they talk about stuff<br /> <br /> Mind and Life are sepparate Spheres in the rules. We have to work with that, barring a major change on the system that I don't think it's warranted here. Saying that the &quot;nervous system&quot; - clearly part of your biology - it's part of the &quot;Mind Sphere&quot; would generate some oddities in the rules.As shown by your very example:<br /> <br /> Raising Dexterity it's normaly Life 3 (altering the &quot;nervous system&quot; could be the Technomancer's way of doing so, while still using Life. After all, that system it's part of your biology, so, why not?), but apparently you can do it much better with Mind from now on, as Mind 1 it's enough to raise Mental Attributes. IDK if one wants to allow that kind of thing</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yes, I failed to express myself properly. Yes, in the D10 system - and most RPGs in general, Dexterity (Agility, Reflex, Speed, whatever you wanna call it) is a physical attribute.<br /> <br /> I just wanted to clear it out that irl the part relative to reflexes is actually closer to perception - there's even a term in the military that I dont recall right now, something like &quot;observe, react&quot;... OOAC or something like that.<br /> <br /> Indeed by the game mechanics DX would fall under Life, but if it were in reality it would probably fall under Mind instead.<br /> <br /> Edit: by the way I do use that on my games. Life is used for Strenght, Endurance and Appereance. Mind 1 can raise all others - Per, Wits, Int, Cha, Man AND Dexterity, it all goes to Mind 1 in my games - and that has never been a problem.<br /> <br /> But that's my house rule obviously. I just find it to better model reality.<br /> <br /> About &quot;nervous system&quot;, our entire &quot;mind&quot; is the nervous system. That would be the same as simply fusing Mind and Life Spheres - which actually wouldnt be a problem for me, 'cause I already play with modified Spheres anyway, because I play WoD adapted on Gurps, so all my Spheres are custom made and unique to the worldview of each group. But at a principle, Dexterity would be a measure of reflex, which is totally mental. But hey, Im not imposing that on any one, just sharing my 2 cents","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24689,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","user":"Kakost","date":". 07-14-2022, 03:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-14T12:53:32-07:00","id":1486456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1486341-mind-sphere-increasing-ability-scores?p=1486436#post1486436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I did a poor job of pointing out the paradox of creating knowledge in my previous post, let me try with a parable:<br /> <br /> Say you want to conjure an apple. Easy, you know apples, their flavor, shape, and texture.<br /> <br /> Now, I tell you to conjure a kumquat, and let's assume you never heard of kumquats, let alone ate one, or even know what the hell they are. I would say you could not cast that simple conjuration, because you wouldn't even be able to understand what I want. The magic itself doesn't know, your spell doesn't have a target you can Will into.<br /> <br /> Taking that example to knowledge, how are you going to create the knowledge of, say, martial arts if you don't know about martial arts in the first place? Even if you know basics (Brawl 3) and want to increase that, <i>how would you know what you want to be able to know</i>?<br /> <br /> <br /> You can? Either we have a very different interpretation of Entropy, or I'm missing a reference in the books you have and I do not. Entropy 5 + Mind (for me) is affecting conceptual thoughts in a manner that is consistent with Fate or, well, entropy. Changing outlooks, supercharging creativity, inspirations, and so on.<br /> <br /> Edit: Oh i see, you're using Entropy 5 to basically re-invent everything on the fly based on what you know already. That could work I guess, but would probably be a pretty steep roll.<br /> <br /> I agree though that once you have a source for the knowledge, it becomes much easier to Will it into your brain.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, in theory a Mage with Entropy 5 could create knowledge out of thin air, even if that knowledge is completely alien to the mage... Supose our Fate Master wanted to learn about Sphributs, but he never ever heard about that word he just made up... Well, he cast his magick hand and Voila! The knowledge is built. All of a sudden, it just so happens that he now knows about the ephemeral Sphributs spirits (probably in this case Destiny itself would be creating those in the spot).<br /> <br /> Or, in a more tangible example thou, lets imagine that master Xander, a 11th century persian mage, who is a master of both Time and Entropy, decided to take a trip to the future.<br /> <br /> All of a sudden - Behold! He is faced with a magic mirror filled with arcane and constantly shifting symbols, being used by what seems to be a commoner of the 21th century.<br /> <br /> Now, master Xander could in theory use Entropy 5 to understand what the hell a computer is, even if that is an alien artifact for him.<br /> <br /> That's.... hard thou. Very very hard.<br /> <br /> It's not what my VA or Iteration X do however, thus would be too hard and too vain to accomplish.<br /> <br /> What they do is much simpler, it is to run up computer simulations that add up knowledge based on previously acessed knowledge (ie this is their technobabble explation for the effect).<br /> <br /> This works even for something like &quot;Knowledge about the Camarilla&quot; for example. If you know a few key factors, using probabilistic analyzes (ie Entropy 5) you can construct the entire landscape of the field. Or for example, if you know a little about physics, you can deduce Quantum Mechanics. That's more or less how it works.<br /> <br /> But yes, in game terms it's all Entropy 5","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-14T13:28:04-07:00","id":1486459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1486341-mind-sphere-increasing-ability-scores?p=1486440#post1486440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Absolutely, You need to know what you create. Trying to Mind 3/Prime 2 knowledge would be futile<br /> <br /> That being said, magick could be able to procure knowledge, if you know where to search, and, as you said &amp;quot;blast your brain&amp;quot; with it (or otherwise incorporate). Several examples were given. Like the &amp;quot;copy it from another&amp;quot; example: I don't know much martial arts, but will trust the famous Sifu down there knows. That's how normal people gains those dots - magick would just resolve the mundane ways in a different fashion<br /> <br /> I would add that maybe you can extract knowledge from the High Umbra, with Cosmology and a bit of knowledge on the subject to seek the right realms. That may be one way to gain levels above 5 (something rather hard to find in other people). Albeit I would imagine it would take arround Mind 4 (or maybe less, with some Spirit)</div> </div> </div> </div>In my games I have both the Abyss and the Oblivion being &quot;final destinations&quot; for everything - including thoughts. This means that you could - in theory - acess ALL knowledge of the Tellurian - including future knowledge! (since in my game, those two places are like &quot;spiritual black holes&quot; that exist outside of time itself, thus they contain the residual thoughts of EVERYTHING from both past, present and future). So, a Spirit 2 while there could in theory open up open every single possible knowledge in existance.<br /> <br /> The truth is thou, that even if you could survive such a trip (an unlikely proposition at best), the endless cacophony of thoughts would probably drive you mad before achieving enlightment.<br /> <br /> I do use it for my games thou - if you use Spirit 2, Entropy 2 and Correspondence 2 to &quot;briefly&quot; touch the Abyss/Oblivion, you can gain forbidden knowledge (Spirit 2 is obviously to &quot;connect&quot; with the spirit world, Corres. is because neither the Abyss or Oblivion are in the Penumbra, so you need to project your magick all the way down there, and Entropy 2 is to &quot;filter&quot; the endless cesspool of vanished thoughts).<br /> <br /> This is something that is mostly one done by Nefandi or Marauders thou. Forbidden knowledge tends to be forbidden for a reason.<br /> <br /> But yes, my games have those main sources of skills. For VAs and the Technos, they have extensive digital mental libraries, so it's a kind of a &quot;group background&quot;, more or less like Nosferatus are always well informed because it's their &quot;culture&quot;. If you're a VA geek who never fought in your life, you can just simply download Martial Arts mastery from their Node on the digital web. It works like in the Matrix &quot;Operator, please download me operation of F35 jets&quot;, and it's done, because they have all of those stored. Other traditions have &quot;crystal memories&quot; and such similar, but no one else have such an extensive or organized collection as the technoboys and VAs have. And, Nefandi, Marauders and Hubristic mages access a dangerous endless source of knowledge.<br /> <br /> The astral plane can also be &quot;farmed&quot; with similar purpose, but it aint so easy or direct as the Abyss or Oblivion. But it's a lot safer to find knowledge in the astral plane than risking corruption/infection by the Oblivion or Abyss","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-15T23:31:54-07:00","id":1486593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1486341-mind-sphere-increasing-ability-scores?p=1486455#post1486455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Indeed by the game mechanics DX would fall under Life, but if it were in reality it would probably fall under Mind instead.<br /> <br /> Edit: by the way I do use that on my games. Life is used for Strenght, Endurance and Appereance. Mind 1 can raise all others - Per, Wits, Int, Cha, Man AND Dexterity, it all goes to Mind 1 in my games - and that has never been a problem.<br /> <br /> But that's my house rule obviously. I just find it to better model reality.<br /> <br /> About &quot;nervous system&quot;, our entire &quot;mind&quot; is the nervous system. That would be the same as simply fusing Mind and Life Spheres - which actually wouldnt be a problem for me, 'cause I already play with modified Spheres anyway, because I play WoD adapted on Gurps, so all my Spheres are custom made and unique to the worldview of each group. But at a principle, Dexterity would be a measure of reflex, which is totally mental. But hey, Im not imposing that on any one, just sharing my 2 cents</div> </div> </div> </div>Ironically, this just makes the Akashic brotherhoods theming easier to digest.<br /> <br /> I bet $5 everyone here has asked why the kung-fu wizards have Mind as their primary sphere. We all know Now that it has to do with the perceptions and philosophies of eastern thought(primarily buddhist and daoist), but it it takes some homework to figure out.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, if mind plays into <i>The</i> most important combat stat(Dex), then the kung-fu wizards make more sense on a person's first reading.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-16T07:52:21-07:00","id":1486620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1486341-mind-sphere-increasing-ability-scores?p=1486593#post1486593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ironically, this just makes the Akashic brotherhoods theming easier to digest.<br /> <br /> I bet $5 everyone here has asked why the kung-fu wizards have Mind as their primary sphere. We all know Now that it has to do with the perceptions and philosophies of eastern thought(primarily buddhist and daoist), but it it takes some homework to figure out.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, if mind plays into <i>The</i> most important combat stat(Dex), then the kung-fu wizards make more sense on a person's first reading.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow, good call, despite already using that as my own personal home rule, I had never thought about how fitting that is for them - probably because I never had a player play an Akashic. I have STed many Technos games thou, and it's awesome for the boys in black suits to use Mind for &quot;Agility and Reflexes&quot;, this has always worked out very well for my NWO guys - but yes, you're right, it represents a massive fitting improvement for the Akashics","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-17T00:24:10-07:00","id":1486726,"title":"","content":"Made a mistake.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-26T21:41:52-07:00","id":1488131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1486341-mind-sphere-increasing-ability-scores?p=1486593#post1486593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ironically, this just makes the Akashic brotherhoods theming easier to digest.<br /> <br /> I bet $5 everyone here has asked why the kung-fu wizards have Mind as their primary sphere. We all know Now that it has to do with the perceptions and philosophies of eastern thought(primarily buddhist and daoist), but it it takes some homework to figure out.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, if mind plays into <i>The</i> most important combat stat(Dex), then the kung-fu wizards make more sense on a person's first reading.</div> </div> </div> </div>Teeeechnically, Mind would make perfect sense for the Akashics - but the reason is indeed better represented with a raise of an Ability (Martial Arts, Do) instead of an Attribute (Dex). Maybe.<br /> <br /> The big, gamechanging difference in a conflict between an experienced martial artist (Or general fighter, swordsman, marksman, whatever physically tricky and rapid skill) and an inexperienced one isn't necessarily strength, or agility, or technique or what have you; The key difference is that the inexperienced actor has to think about what they're doing, constantly. They gotta remember things, or frantically think about how to react, etc. etc., which is why they're slower and make mistakes and struggle.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile the experienced, trained person (to oversimply it just a bit) just *does*. It's ingrained and on automatic. It's not that they're not thinking about what they're doing, but the decision making is just very fast triggers or even pure reflex. It's why they're faster, more coordinated and calculating - ironically by having to calculate less. A big part of mastering a lot of physical things is training the brain and automatic &quot;muscle memory&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> Or, to put it simple, an inexperienced juggler goes 'okay leftrighttmovethehandohthatoneisoffmovefasterwhewg otitohdamndamnalmost' while the very experienced one can talk about their next vacation plans with you while they're performing.<br /> <br /> <br /> So, Mind for the Akashics combat makes very much sense (outside of it making sense for the whole ordered and calm mind philosophy of their bhuddism-like approach) - it's just a question of how to represent it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 07-28-2022, 10:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-27T08:54:29-07:00","id":1488174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1486341-mind-sphere-increasing-ability-scores?p=1488131#post1488131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Teeeechnically, Mind would make perfect sense for the Akashics - but the reason is indeed better represented with a raise of an Ability (Martial Arts, Do) instead of an Attribute (Dex). Maybe.<br /> <br /> The big, gamechanging difference in a conflict between an experienced martial artist (Or general fighter, swordsman, marksman, what physically tricky and rapid skill) and an inexperienced one isn't necessarily strength, or agility, or technique or what have you; The key difference is that the inexperienced actor has to think about what they're doing, constantly. They gotta remember things, or frantically think about how to react, etc. etc., which is why they're slower and make mistakes and struggle.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile the experienced, trained person (to oversimply it just a bit) just *does*. It's ingrained and on automatic. It's not that they're not thinking about what they're doing, but the decision making is just very fast triggers or even pure reflex. It's why they're faster, more coordinated and calculating - ironically by having to calculate less. A big part of mastering a lot of physical things is training the brain and automatic &amp;quot;muscle memory&amp;quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> Or, to put it simple, an inexperienced juggler goes 'okay leftrighttmovethehandohthatoneisoffmovefasterwhewg otitohdamndamnalmost' while the very experienced one can talk about their next vacation plans with you while they're performing.<br /> <br /> <br /> So, Mind for the Akashics combat makes very much sense (outside of it making sense for the whole ordered and calm mind philosophy of their bhuddism-like approach) - it's just a question of how to represent it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, like I said dexterity is a measure of reflex, which is about the brain, not muscles. So, irl is a reflection of mental training, not muscular power or bone mass. <br /> <br /> Now, &quot;reflexes&quot; would be the &quot;attribute&quot;; a basketball player has good reflexes; it doesnt mean he's a kung fu master, and likewise a kung fu master aint a NBA player. And here is where enter the skill, which is a measure of accumulated knowledge - Sports for the NBA player, Martial Arts for the fighter. And for that part too, Mind fits like a glove - just Mind 3 &quot;borrow&quot; the kung fu/karate from the Sifu/Sensei - or like I said, &quot;print it&quot; into the Tradition tomes with Prime 4. Need a quick temporary boost to your Martial Arts? Ok, just read THAT scroll.<br /> <br /> Mind 1 also helps with focus (clear your mind of all distractions, padawan), which should at the very least reduce the difficulties - even for martial arts","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-01T13:15:48-07:00","id":1488730,"title":"","content":"I have a mage who is a popstar/actress, and her specialty is mind. The way we handle this is she has a rote called &quot;I'm not a doctor but I play one on tv&quot; She basically embodies a &quot;role&quot; and then gains the skills associated with that role. If she needs medicine, she embodies the role of doctor. If she needs to fight, she embodies the role of Action hero. And then we divy up the dots she gets based on her successes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26766-mezlabor","name":"mezlabor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}